You are assisting with business process modelling. A first check could not decide whether the conditions in the list below hold for the business process described below. They are conditions of the rule [GDPR-Art13-4]. Look again.

INSTRUCTIONS
- The legal passages below are all the rules found for this process. Use them only to understand what a condition means (for example a definition of a word). Whether a condition holds must still be shown by the process description.
- For each condition, choose its status:
  - "confirmed": the description states that it holds. A statement in legal terms is "confirmed" when the description states the same fact in everyday words.
  - "contradicted": the description states something that makes it false.
  - "not_stated": use this only when no sentence of the description speaks to the statement.
- "confirmed" needs a quote that itself states that fact; a sentence about a different event never confirms it.
- Do not guess facts the description does not state.
- quotes: for "confirmed" or "contradicted", a list of 1 to 3 sentences of the process description that together show it, each copied exactly and word for word. Use more than one sentence only when the fact is stated across several sentences. For "not_stated", use an empty list []. Quotes are checked automatically; a quote that does not appear in the description is ignored, and an item with no such quote counts as "not_stated".
- Give one result for every condition, with its id, and no other results.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

EXAMPLE OF EVERYDAY WORDS (made up, from another domain)
Statement: "C1: the vessel has obtained clearance for departure from the port authority"
Description sentence: "The harbour master tells the captain that the ship may leave."
Result: "confirmed", quotes ["The harbour master tells the captain that the ship may leave"] (the same fact in everyday words). The sentence "The crew loads the cargo." speaks about a different event and would not confirm it.

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "ItemCheck": {
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "description": "The id of the item, as given in the list",
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "closest_sentence": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "The sentence of the process description that comes closest to the statement, copied word for word, or null if none",
          "title": "Closest Sentence"
        },
        "status": {
          "description": "confirmed, contradicted or not_stated, judged from the description only",
          "enum": [
            "confirmed",
            "not_stated",
            "contradicted"
          ],
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "quotes": {
          "description": "1 to 3 sentences copied word for word from the process description that together show the status; empty list for not_stated",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "maxItems": 3,
          "title": "Quotes",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "closest_sentence",
        "status",
        "quotes"
      ],
      "title": "ItemCheck",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "results": {
      "description": "One result for every item of the list",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/ItemCheck"
      },
      "title": "Results",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "results"
  ],
  "title": "CheckOutputV2",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
This process begins when a potential customer inquires about a product or service.
Sales staff or customer support collects relevant information and addresses any concerns or questions.
If the customer is interested, they are guided through selecting the appropriate product or service.
Next, the sales representative provides a quote, and after approval from the customer, the process moves to order placement.
The order is then recorded in the system, and the customer receives confirmation of their order.
The process ends when the order is successfully placed and confirmed.
The company is based in Germany and sells to customers across the EU. During the inquiry, the sales staff write down the customer's name, phone number and email address and store them in the system.

LEGAL PASSAGES
[GDPR-Art13-1] General Data Protection Regulation (2016/679) - Article 13: Information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject
1. Where personal data relating to a data subject are collected from the data subject, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with all of the following information:
(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller and, where applicable, of the controller's representative;
(b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable;
(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended as well as the legal basis for the processing;
(d) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1), the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party;
(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any;
(f) where applicable, the fact that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation and the existence or absence of an adequacy decision by the Commission, or in the case of transfers referred to in Article 46 or 47, or the second subparagraph of Article 49(1), reference to the appropriate or suitable safeguards and the means by which to obtain a copy of them or where they have been made available.

[GDPR-Art13-2-a] General Data Protection Regulation (2016/679) - Article 13: Information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject
2. In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing:
(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or if that is not possible, the criteria used to determine that period;
(b) the existence of the right to request from the controller access to and rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing concerning the data subject or to object to processing as well as the right to data portability;
(c) where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal;
(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
(e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, or a requirement necessary to enter into a contract, as well as whether the data subject is obliged to provide the personal data and of the possible consequences of failure to provide such data;

[GDPR-Art13-2-f] General Data Protection Regulation (2016/679) - Article 13: Information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject
2. In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing:
(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4) and, at least in those cases, meaningful information about the logic involved, as well as the significance and the envisaged consequences of such processing for the data subject.

[GDPR-Art13-3] General Data Protection Regulation (2016/679) - Article 13: Information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject
3. Where the controller intends to further process the personal data for a purpose other than that for which the personal data were collected, the controller shall provide the data subject prior to that further processing with information on that other purpose and with any relevant further information as referred to in paragraph 2.

CONDITIONS
C1: the data subject already has the information

